    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0720" n="710" xml:id="pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.154/366: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-21T15:00:00+07:00">August 21, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 22—6:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>360. For Currie from Arnstein: Generalissimo has decided against Holmes due to
                    his nationality. Present contemplated plan is Chinese managing director with
                        Wilson<anchor n="76" xml:id="d742-f1"/> in complete charge of operation and
                    maintenance of all the lend-lease trucks. Wilson will assume duties as soon as
                    he is released from the Army. [Arnstein.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d742-f1" n="76" xml:id="d742-f1-content">
                <p>Capt. James Wilson, U. S. A., Assistant Military Attaché in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
